  {"path":"/api/admin/admin-profiles/[id]","guard":"session","methods":["PUT","DELETE"],"permission":"admin_profiles:manage","sameOrigin":true,"note":"404 with RBAC_PERMISSIONS_ENABLED off; each write is the confirmed Root's with step-up (requireRootPower, else 403 root_only), same-origin JSON (DELETE carries the password); built-in profiles are read-only; a profile an admin holds is never deleted (409 profile_in_use); a removal raises its admins' session version and closes their sockets (step 3.11)"},
  {"path":"/api/admin/instance-settings","guard":"session","methods":["GET","PUT"],"sameOrigin":true,"note":"getSession (fresh for the PUT) reads the signed-in account, never the act-as one; 404 with RBAC_IDENTITY_ENABLED off; an admin reads and changes everything (a capture change only holding platform:traffic_capture, every admin with RBAC_PERMISSIONS_ENABLED off), the tunnels legacy holder or a compat account only the tunnel (sharedToolAccess tunnels, HD-06, OQ-R3 (a)), anyone else 403 instance:settings; PUT same-origin JSON only (ID-32, step 2.4); the security policy fields (password policy, lifetimes, impersonation, publicBaseUrl) change only by the confirmed Root with step-up, anyone else 403 root_only (step 2.6)"},
