  {"path":"/api/admin/permission-sets/[id]","guard":"session","methods":["PUT","DELETE"],"permission":"roles:manage","sameOrigin":true,"note":"404 with RBAC_PERMISSIONS_ENABLED off; roles:manage, same-origin; PUT adds only permissions the editor holds (PE-11; a cross-tenant tool, an exploitation approval, sessions or Kali exec take step-up), instanceDefault is instance:settings: the confirmed Root's with step-up, else 403 root_only; built-ins are read-only; DELETE refused while anyone holds the set or it is the instance default (409, PE-17); a removal raises the holders' session version and closes their sockets (step 3.11)"},
